==Battleground==
*1 [[UltraBaaBaa]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[J.K. Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 8.33~16.67 seconds<sup>250f~500f</sup>.
*15 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*5 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*5 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 8.33 seconds<sup>250f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Brollow]]s spawn after 140 seconds<sup>4,200f</sup>, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
First, note that this stage is almost impossible unless you have a way to break UltraBaaBaa's [[Barrier]], which has the same breaking point as [[Youcan]]'s Barrier (266,000). There's only one UltraBaaBaa, so any [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breaker]] or the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast Cannon]] will be enough. For the rest, bring some meatshields and peon clearers, focus your army to counter [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] (namely by bringing [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] and maybe [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]]) and you won't have issues here. With a bit of help, [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] can defeat J.K. Bun Bun before the Brollows arrive, trivializing the stage.

==Trivia==
*Wearable Homes is presumably named after [[wikipedia:Wearable technology|wearable technology]], since most [[Singularityville]] stages have technology-related names.
**It could also refer to [[Wikipedia:Hermit crab|Hermit crabs]], which wear "mobile shelters" (usually shells) to protect themselves. This is reinforced by the beach background and beach-themed enemy base. Ironically, there is not a single [[Helmut Krabbe]] in Wearable Homes.
***UltraBaaBaa, who debuts here, may be the stand-in for hermit crabs as her barrier could be considered a "wearable home"

